From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: tve: register the connector as Composite

The TV encoder outputs CVBS alone, yet registered its connector as TV,
the type for an output that switches among composite, S-Video and
component. Composite is the type for CVBS, as sunxi's, meson's and
vc4's encoders register it, so userspace and the command line name it
Composite-1 on every SoC.

The boot logo's hand-over keeps a reference for outputs that support
hot-plug, TV among them: Composite joins it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
@@ -1110,7 +1110,7 @@
 	connector->interlace_allowed = 1;
 	ret = drm_connector_init(drm_dev, connector,
 				 &rockchip_tve_connector_funcs,
-				 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_TV);
+				 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Composite);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_dbg(tve->dev, "failed to initialize connector with drm\n");
 		goto err_free_encoder;
diff -urN a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA:
 	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIB:
 	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_TV:
+	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Composite:
 		return true;
 	default:
 		return false;
